   "final_text": "The feed had one event, a new hire, and it's fully handled. The feed has now been quiet for about 50 minutes and nothing I started is still pending.\n\n**Samira Qureshi (E1025), Software Engineer, start date 2026-11-02, case case-9c4a67c3**\n- **Same person or not:** Two former workers share her name: E1023 (Software Engineer) and E1024 (Sales Rep). Her new record had no government ID token and no link to an earlier record, so I couldn't tell who she was. I asked HR, and they confirmed she is the same person as E1024.\n- **Identity:** Our policy is that a returning employee keeps their old account and doesn't get their old access back. So I moved her old account `acct-94d2c3a6` (samira.qureshi2@example.com) onto the new worker record as an Employee. I then:\n  - set up a new user mailbox (the old shared mailbox was left as it was);\n  - added only the standard Software Engineer groups (All-Staff, VPN-Users, Eng-Git), after checking they don't break any segregation-of-duties rules;\n  - turned the account on. Her start date is today, so she doesn't have access early.\n- **Work email in Workday:** I wrote samira.qureshi2@example.com back to her Workday record. The update finished successfully and the record now shows it. The one other event in the feed (seq 2) was just the confirmation of that update.\n- **Finance:** I created her finance profile with cost center CC-1000 and her manager Jordan Carter (E1001) as expense approver.\n- **Equipment:** I ordered the engineering laptop bundle (ticket `tkt-4a21f703`, still open for delivery).\n- **Workday onboarding tasks:** Both are marked Complete (\"Create accounts and email\" and \"Provision equipment\").\n\nThe only human input needed was HR's one-time confirmation of who she was."
